\DOC distinctness_store

\TYPE {distinctness_store : (string * (unit -> thm)) list ref}

\SYNOPSIS
Internal list of distinctness theorems, each proved when first needed.

\DESCRIBE
This list associates with the name of each recursive type defined so far that
has at least two constructors a function returning its distinctness theorem
(see {distinctness}). The theorem is proved when the function is first called,
and saved for later calls, so it is never proved for types where it is not
used; it has a conjunct for each pair of constructors, so for types with many
constructors this saves much time and space. The list is automatically
extended by {define_type} and used by {distinctness}.

\FAILURE
Not applicable.

\EXAMPLE
{
  # assoc "list" (!distinctness_store);;
  val it : unit -> thm = <fun>

  # assoc "list" (!distinctness_store) ();;
  val it : thm = |- !a0' a1'. ~([] = CONS a0' a1')
}

\SEEALSO
constructors_distinct_net, define_type, distinctness, extend_rectype_net,
injectivity_store.

\ENDDOC
